  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Interior Design Questionnaire FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an interior design questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"An interior design questionnaire is the set of questions a designer sends a new client before the first consultation. It asks who lives in the home, which rooms are in the project, what furniture stays, the client's style, the budget, and the timeline. The answers become the designer's starting brief before anyone visits.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an interior design questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Start with the decisions the answers must settle, then group the questions by room. Describe that structure to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> in plain English, including the photo uploads and any rule, such as marking fabric for homes with pets. It builds the form and a database for the answers. Try it with a past client's details before the first real send.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an interior design questionnaire template include?\", \"a\": \"Five parts: contact details and the property address, the household with pets and children's ages, the rooms in scope with photos, the furniture that stays, and the budget with a target finish date. Put style questions after the practical ones. If you start from an interior design questionnaire PDF, keep its sections but move them into a form where each photo arrives filed under its room.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a commercial interior design questionnaire ask about the client's brand?\", \"a\": \"Ask for the logo, the brand colors with their codes, the typefaces, and three words the space should feel like to a visitor. In a shop or a restaurant, those answers steer the finishes and the signage. If the client is still working out the brand itself, send a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/brand-questionnaire'>brand questionnaire</a> first and design the space once it is settled.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I ask about budget in an interior design questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Ask for one total, then ask what it covers: furniture and decor only, or the construction work as well. Two clients who both write $40,000 can be describing two different projects until that line is answered. Ask whether the figure is firm or a starting point, and save the per-room split for later in the form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long should an interior design questionnaire be?\", \"a\": \"Keep it short enough to finish in one sitting; about 25 questions plus photos is a workable ceiling. Leave anything you learn faster in person, such as how a fabric feels or how loud a room is, for the consultation. Emergent builds the form from a prompt, and cutting a section later is a one-line change to that prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should a client fill out an interior design questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Before the first consultation. Reading the answers first lets the consultation start from the client's photos and budget instead of a blank page. After the client signs, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/client-onboarding-questionnaire'>client onboarding questionnaire</a> collects what the job itself needs, such as access instructions and who approves invoices.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an office interior design questionnaire ask clients?\", \"a\": \"Ask how the office is used, not only how big the team is. Beyond total staff and the busiest-day count, ask which teams sit together and how many meeting rooms are booked at peak. Then ask where people take calls and how much the headcount should grow during the lease. The app Emergent builds can send each response to any project tool with an API.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can clients upload room photos and measurements in an interior design questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Each room section can take photos and wall measurements, and the uploads save with that room's answers. Ask for daylight photos from the doorway and one straight-on shot of each window wall, with the window width noted. A questionnaire built with Emergent has no response caps, which matters in the months when inquiries pile up.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a one-room refresh get the same interior design questionnaire as a full home?\", \"a\": \"No. A full-home questionnaire asks far more than a single-room job needs. For one-off work such as a bedroom refresh or styling a bookshelf wall, a short <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/project-request'>project request form</a> with photos of the room and a budget gives you enough to quote.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "afb---prompt": "<p>Build an interior design questionnaire that saves every response to a database I own.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build an interior design questionnaire that saves every response to a database I own.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Rooms in Scope\", \"add\": \"Add questions for each room in scope, and skip the rooms the client leaves out.\"}, {\"label\": \"Photo Uploads\", \"add\": \"Add photo uploads for every room and for each piece of furniture the client owns.\"}, {\"label\": \"Style Picks\", \"add\": \"Add style picks where the client chooses between pairs of room photos.\"}, {\"label\": \"Budget by Room\", \"add\": \"Add a budget by room that adds up against the total the client enters.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
